// W-WINOPTS stage 1 (docs/APP-WINDOW-OPTS.md): the window's own opacity, 0..255 (255 = opaque, the default). The window must be
// the caller's own (the handle says so); a value above 255 is refused with E_INVALID, never clamped. WI_OPAC reads it back.
const WS_OPAC: u64 = 7
// The window options word: argument a3 of WM_CREATE (bit 0 is the old `kind` bit). The options take effect BEFORE the window opens,
// so a frameless window never shows a frame, not even for one picture. Any bit outside WO_KNOWN is refused (E_INVALID) and no
// window is made. Layer is NOT in the word (stage 2: L_FLOAT, with the right `window.float`).
const WO_FRAMELESS: u64 = 2 // no frame and no title bar (the same as WS_DECO 0)
